{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who is like You among the gods, etc.</b> The meaning is: since we see Egypt — that is, the sar of Egypt, whose name is Met — who is like HaShem among the sons of the mighty?" "<b>Further,</b> it appears according to the saying of our Sages of blessed memory (Ḥagigah 16a): a king of flesh and blood, when he hides among the people, is not recognized as being that one — unlike our Elohim, who is a sign in His host. And this is what the verse says: <b>who is like You</b> — even when You are among the gods without any mark of royalty being imprinted, [Your majesty] is still imprinted." "<b>Further,</b> it intends according to the saying of our Sages of blessed memory (Mekhilta): a king of flesh and blood — his fear is upon those who are far more than upon those who are near, but the Holy One, blessed be He — His fear is upon those who are near more, etc. And this is what it says: <b>who is like You among the gods</b> — for there [among the upper beings] they recognize [You] more. But among the lower beings — when is <b>who is like You</b>? — when You are adorned in holiness, when You grant strength and majesty to the aspect of holiness, as in the deed of the land of Egypt, which humbled the pride of wickedness and exalted holiness." "<b>Further,</b> it intends according to the verse: ״נְהַר דִּינוּר נָגֵד וְנָפִיק מִן קֳדָמוֹהִי״ (Daniel 7:10), and our Sages of blessed memory said (Ḥagigah 13a) that from the perspiration of the ḥayot when they sweat at the time they say קָדוֹשׁ, the river Dinur goes forth. And this is what it says: <b>adorned in holiness</b> — meaning, when they exalt Him in holiness, then, on account of the awe that enters the ḥayot when they praise Him, that Awesome One performs [wonders], that they sweat the river Dinur." "<b>Awesome in praises, doing wonders, etc.</b> The meaning is: everyone ought to fear to tell His praises, since all His deeds are wondrous, and who is the one who would presume to be precise in His praises? For no man can grasp the wondrous knowledge to praise Him fittingly. And how could they praise Him at a small level, given that He possesses a wondrous, concealed attribute of greatness and might."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:32.362105305Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}